OVERVIEW: Organize and analyze DICOM studies and series

Manage DICOM studies with organization, summarization, validation, and
statistics.
Supports study/series organization, completeness checking, and comparison.

Files are grouped by Study Instance UID (0020,000D) and
Series Instance UID (0020,000E), the unique keys of the Study and Series
levels (PS3.4 C.6.1.1).

Examples:
  dicom-study organize files/ --output organized/
  dicom-study summary study/ --format table
  dicom-study check study/ --expected-series 5 --report missing.txt
  dicom-study stats study/ --detailed
  dicom-study compare study1/ study2/ --format json

USAGE: dicom-study <subcommand>

OPTIONS:
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

SUBCOMMANDS:
  organize                Organize DICOM files by study and series hierarchy
  summary                 Display study and series metadata summary
  check                   Check study completeness: series and instance counts,
                          and gaps in Instance Number (0020,0013)
  stats                   Calculate study statistics and metrics
  compare                 Compare two studies for differences

  See 'dicom-study help <subcommand>' for detailed help.
